# How the decompiled NemesisMod class is split into partial files.
#
# One line per file: <Topic> <first method>. A file takes every method from its
# first method up to the next file's first method, in metadata order (the order
# the author's own partial files were compiled in - see docs/RECONSTRUCTION.md).
# Topic "-" is the core file NemesisMod.cs. A method name resolves to its first
# occurrence after the previous line's method, so overloads are fine.
#
#   = <Topic> <member>   moves one method or property to another file
#
# Fields and nested types follow automatically (tools/Splitter: declaration
# order + who uses them + the recovered field-block positions).

